.TH SDXI_CXT 3
.SH NAME
sdxi_cxt \- SDXI context lifecycle and control-plane helpers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <sdxi/cxt.h>

struct sdxi_cxt_create_opts {
        uint32_t size;
        uint32_t flags;
        uint32_t ds_ring_entries;
        uint32_t opb_000_enb;
        int eventfd;
        uint32_t rsvd[8];
};

int sdxi_cxt_create(sdxi_dev_t *dev,
                    const struct sdxi_cxt_create_opts *opts,
                    sdxi_cxt_t **cxt_out);
int sdxi_cxt_quiesce(sdxi_cxt_t *cxt, uint32_t timeout_ms,
                     uint32_t *cst_flags_out);
int sdxi_cxt_destroy(sdxi_cxt_t *cxt);

uint32_t sdxi_cxt_pasid(const sdxi_cxt_t *cxt);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
An
.B sdxi_cxt_t
is a local userspace context object. It owns the context fd returned by the
driver and any mappings or auxiliary buffers the library creates.
.PP
The
.BR sdxi/cxt.h
header is the control-plane half of the context API. It keeps lifecycle
operations and PASID introspection here, while raw local context-fd and mmap
accessors live in
.BR sdxi_dp (3)
as part of the advanced local dataplane boundary.
.PP
Creation options support:
.TP
.B SDXI_CXT_CREATE_F_EVENTFD
request a context eventfd during creation
.PP
When
.I opts
is NULL, libsdxi uses default options. When
.I opts
is non-NULL,
.I size
may be 0 or
.BR "sizeof(struct sdxi_cxt_create_opts)" .
Unknown flags and reserved fields must be zero.
.PP
The
.I opb_000_enb
field is a raw SDXI opb_000 mask: bit N requests opcode type N for types
0 through 31. A value of 0 requests the driver default. Function-assigned
opcode types are discovered with
.BR sdxi_dev_admin_disc ()
or
.BR sdxi_dev_get_op_type ().
The driver checks the requested mask against device availability and context
policy; discovering a group does not authorize its use.
.PP
If
.B SDXI_CXT_CREATE_F_EVENTFD
is set and
.I eventfd
is -1, libsdxi creates and owns an eventfd. If
.I eventfd
is non-negative, the caller owns the fd.
.PP
.BR sdxi_cxt_quiesce ()
is the explicit stop boundary.
.BR sdxi_cxt_destroy ()
will call
.BR sdxi_cxt_quiesce ()
if needed, then tear down mappings and close owned resources.
.SH NOTES
Only the local backend is supported for
.BR sdxi_cxt_t .
The object is not transport-neutral and should not be treated as something a
remote or non-local backend can impersonate.
.PP
There is no public post-create context-eventfd setter.
If
.BR sdxi_cxt_create ()
is called with a NULL options pointer, the library uses its default ring size,
currently 1024 entries.
.PP
Context creation allocates userspace ring/status buffers and locks them with
.BR mlock (2)
before passing their addresses to the kernel. If context creation fails with
.B ENOMEM
even though the device can be opened, check the process
.B RLIMIT_MEMLOCK
or grant an appropriate capability such as
.BR CAP_IPC_LOCK .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDXI (7),
.BR sdxi_event (3),
.BR sdxi_dp (3),
.BR sdxi_key (3)
